From 9fc8c251a7808add4407a9c68455821a25a4f52a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:12:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] WIP: mailbox fuzz oracle reads messages in the library's
 order

The wormhole_mailbox target now restates how magic-wormhole 0.8.1 takes
peer messages -- by arrival, skipping its own echoes and phases already
taken -- and asserts the message in each place is safe there (kept[12]).
A dictionary token for the side the harness binds as, and seeds for an
honest exchange with echoes and for the W3 two-message attack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ENZSCiAud5Vs29ugEacpyR
